{"_type":"issue","id":"cce-data-delivery-validator-ven","title":"Standard-revision proposals: schemaVersion identity, no-runtime-fetch, content-hash manifest","description":"Upstream suggestions for the next WHO-stewarded revision of the Interoperable CCE Data Delivery schema/standard. Not blocking v1 (our tool handles today's ambiguity via normalization — see DESIGN.md §9), but worth proposing since the standard is being revised.\n\nProposals:\n1. Make meta.schemaVersion an explicit, opaque bare-semver token (e.g. \"0.8.0\") and state in prose it is an identifier the receiver maps to a schema via its own registry — decoupled from hosting. Drop the 'see the $id field' phrasing that conflates identifier with locator.\n2. State that receivers MUST NOT dereference the schema at validation time and SHOULD validate against a pre-registered copy (availability, SSRF, and provability reasons).\n3. Mechanically link $id and schemaVersion so there is exactly one version string and a deterministic way to derive one from the other.\n4. Publish an out-of-band manifest with a content hash (sha256) per version, so any receiver can prove it holds the blessed bytes.\n5. Fix the stale example: schemaVersion.examples is \"0.1.1\" (annotation-only, ignored by validators). Must be fixed upstream, NOT in our vendored copy, since we pin that file by content hash (DESIGN.md §9).\n\nContext: DESIGN.md §9 (schema registry) and §15 (deferred).","status":"open","priority":3,"issue_type":"task","owner":"benson.miller@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-05-30T00:17:11Z","created_by":"Benson Miller","updated_at":"2026-05-30T00:17:11Z","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
